{"ok":true,"total":3,"succeeded":3,"failed":0,"concurrency":3,"durationMs":53390,"results":[{"id":"2-night-C","ok":true,"path":"/Users/jhuang/Desktop/JH-Projects/risk3d/_claude/themes-min/2-night-C.png","sourcePath":"/Users/jhuang/.codex/generated_images/01a0e8ce-d0c5-7212-b967-6df4e1963e68/exec-d8f2b9b8-9042-4dad-a214-d504c9ae83e2.png","revisedPrompt":"Create exactly one finished raster image: a tall 9:19.5 smartphone video game screenshot for a fictional game titled “War Table.”\n\nArt direction: minimalist, cohesive, premium “night ink” strategy-board interface, inspired by the clarity of classic world-conquest board games but wholly original. Deep navy background #1b2230 with subtle fine paper grain. A recognizable full world map—North and South America, Europe, Africa, Asia, and Australia—fills most of the screen while retaining generous breathing room. Divide land into clear playable territories using one consistent ultra-thin warm-ivory hairline for every coastline and internal border.\n\nTerritory ownership is communicated ONLY by soft, luminous, low-saturation watercolor washes contained within borders: muted coral, slate blue, pale gold, and sage. The washes glow gently and remain translucent and restrained. Put exactly ONE gameplay mark in each territory: a small readable troop number in an elegant high-contrast serif, centered inside a delicate hairline circle. No other territory icons or marks.\n\nAt the top, show the restrained title “WAR TABLE” and four tiny player-color dots with small ivory counts, spaced elegantly. Use one refined high-contrast serif typeface throughout, reminiscent of Cormorant Garamond. Use gold only for hairline accents, small recurring ring ornaments with a center dot, fine dotted sea-route lines, and the single currently active UI element.\n\nAt the bottom, create one soft rounded pill control containing the readable labels “Place   Attack   Fortify   End”; make “Attack” the one active gold element. Add one separate refined “Blitz” button. Ensure typography is crisp and correctly spelled.\n\nThe whole screen should feel like one unified design system: quiet, elegant, extremely restrained, readable, calm, and atmospheric like a star chart. High detail, polished premium mobile-game screenshot. No device frame, no hands, no perspective mockup, no soldier figures, no seals, no fake characters, no flags, no decorative scenery, no clutter, no extra legends, no watermark.","bytes":2312327,"durationMs":53267,"attempts":1,"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","modelProvider":"openai","reasoningEffort":"low","threadId":"01a0e8ce-d0c5-7212-b967-6df4e1963e68"},{"id":"3-watercolor-A","ok":true,"path":"/Users/jhuang/Desktop/JH-Projects/risk3d/_claude/themes-min/3-watercolor-A.png","sourcePath":"/Users/jhuang/.codex/generated_images/01a0e8ce-d0a4-7030-b81c-b2bdd64ad534/exec-700254ff-5ca6-4811-b4d7-ad3d4930aee3.png","revisedPrompt":"Create exactly one final raster image: a wide 16:9 desktop video game screenshot for “War Table,” a calm premium world-conquest strategy board game in the spirit of classic Risk.\n\nComposition: whole board visible mid-game, generous negative space, warm cream ground. A recognizable world map with the Americas, Europe, Africa, Asia, and Australia, divided into clean territories owned by four players. Minimalist, cohesive design system.\n\nIllustrated watercolor variant: coastlines and every territory border use the same single thin hand-drawn ink line weight, with slight lively natural variation like contemporary editorial illustration. Ownership appears only as soft, low-saturation layered watercolor washes contained inside territory lines: terracotta, sage green, dusty blue, and warm ochre. Include subtle visible brush texture without bleeding across boundaries.\n\nExactly one mark inside each territory: a small readable number, set in one elegant high-contrast serif typeface similar to Cormorant Garamond, centered inside a delicate hairline circle. No other territory symbols. Use the same serif typeface for every text element. Small ring ornaments with a center dot recur sparingly as the sole motif.\n\nShow one selected territory with a subtly stronger outline and a thin gold ring framing its marker. A fine, elegant curved attack arrow points from that selected territory to one neighboring territory. Gold is used only for hairline accents and this single active marker treatment.\n\nBottom interface: quiet spacious bottom area. Separate it from the map with one thin gold hairline rule, interrupted at its exact center by a small ring ornament with center dot. Beneath, a soft rounded pill segmented control reading exactly: “Place   Attack   Fortify   End turn”. The Attack segment is the only active segment and is filled with a soft muted color. Include one small restrained button reading exactly “Blitz”. UI pill has a faint diamond paper texture like a premium personal website. All interface copy must be crisp, correct, and readable.\n\nExtreme restraint. Charming but disciplined. Premium app polish. Clear visual hierarchy, high detail, balanced whitespace, cohesive materials. No soldier figures, no seals, no fake characters, no flags, no decorative scenery clutter, no extra icons, no gradients that look digital, no watermark, no logos beyond the title “War Table”.","bytes":2344672,"durationMs":52421,"attempts":1,"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","modelProvider":"openai","reasoningEffort":"low","threadId":"01a0e8ce-d0a4-7030-b81c-b2bdd64ad534"},{"id":"3-watercolor-C","ok":true,"path":"/Users/jhuang/Desktop/JH-Projects/risk3d/_claude/themes-min/3-watercolor-C.png","sourcePath":"/Users/jhuang/.codex/generated_images/01a0e8ce-d1cd-7933-a806-236b2b511316/exec-3570423d-39d9-4d0e-9842-e9fe6f757e5c.png","revisedPrompt":"Create exactly one final raster image: a tall portrait 9:19.5 smartphone video-game screenshot for a fictional game titled “War Table.” Minimalist, cohesive, premium calm world-conquest strategy board game, reminiscent of classic territory-control board games but visually original.\n\nComposition: warm cream background; the recognizable full world map fills most of the screen with generous breathing room, clearly showing the Americas, Europe, Africa, Asia, and Australia. Divide continents into plausible game territories owned by four players. Use extreme restraint and one consistent fine line weight for every coastline and internal border. Coastlines and borders should be lively hand-drawn dark ink with slight natural variation, contemporary editorial illustration quality.\n\nTerritory ownership is indicated ONLY by soft, low-saturation layered watercolor washes contained inside boundaries: terracotta, sage green, dusty blue, and warm ochre. Gentle visible brush texture, no color bleeding outside territory lines. Exactly ONE mark per territory: a small readable number in an elegant high-contrast serif typeface, centered inside a fine hairline circle. No other territory icons.\n\nTop UI: restrained title “WAR TABLE” and four tiny player-color dots with compact counts, arranged with ample space. The active player dot alone has a thin gold ring around it. Recurring decorative motif is only a tiny ring ornament with a center dot, used sparingly.\n\nBottom UI: one soft rounded horizontal pill control with the readable labels “Place   Attack   Fortify   End”; the single active element is accented with restrained hairline gold. Include one separate compact “Blitz” button. Give the pill a very faint diamond paper texture, sophisticated and subtle, like a premium personal website. All text uses one elegant high-contrast serif family similar to Cormorant Garamond. Gold appears ONLY in fine hairline accents and the single active element.\n\nOverall feel: charming but disciplined, cohesive unified design system, sophisticated premium app screenshot, calm and spacious, high detail, crisp and readable. Illustrated watercolor aesthetic with analog tactility but modern interface precision.\n\nStrict exclusions: no soldiers, no fig